      "content": "Understood, I can expand the guide further:\n\n1. Ensure that the SmartHub is powered on. Typically, this involves pressing the power button located on the side or bottom of the device for about 3 seconds if it's turned off or waiting for the light to indicate it is on.\n2. Insert the USB power adapter firmly into the SmartHub's power port. This can often be a silver or blue box-on-box connector, situated centrally on the front plate.\n3. Connect the device's power cable from the SmartHub to the power adapter. Ensure there is no damage to the cords and that they are firmly connected.\n4. Place the SmartHub in your router to help with signal transmission, side by side with the converter pilot in the same horizontal plane.\n5. Plug the Ethernet cable into the SmartHub's WAN port and the router's WAN port, securing the connections neatly and avoiding bending or dragging the cable on the floor.\n6. Ensure your room is clear of large metal objects or dense materials that may interfere with wireless signals, such as mirrors or metal filing cabinets.\n7. Open a device's settings menu by navigating to the \"Wi-Fi\" or \"Network & Internet\" option. Verify whether Wi-Fi networks appear on the",
